{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1478597730,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTA4OTAzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259089034"},"message":"Hm. It wasn't foreseen to ask a `GitRepo' whether or not a file has content. But I see your point.\n\nThe question to me is: How far is this going to go? Do you want to be able to call `unannex` on a plain git repo, since - well, the result will be okayish? What about `drop` or `get`? Could be done as well.\nBasically everything can be interpreted somehow to fit to both kinds of repos. Is this what we want? To have all methods available from both classes? I'm serious. This would be a major design decision and we better make it soon.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1478598876,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTA5MzI4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259093280"},"message":"One major thing IMHO is code that needs to decide whether something is potentially not here, but could be here. So whenever (without annex peculiarities) would use `exists()` and decide.\n\nI wouldn't not aim for uniformity for uniformity sake. `drop` has no meaning or even utility in Git. Same for many other aspects.\n\nHere is a non-exhaustive list where it would make sense for me:\n- get_file_size\n- file_has_content\n- is_under_annex\n- ...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1478599594,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTA5NjA0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259096047"},"message":"Okay. So, let's grow that list and have a third class, that declares those (abstract). Then `GitRepo` and `AnnexRepo` have to implement them. That way that list would be easy to grow and maintain.\nAnd: I'd like to make it explicit, that these methods are supposed to work on both, while being implemented differently and while, at a first glance, some of them might not really make sense for a `GitRepo`. That's why a dedicated container for these \"result oriented cross repo methods\" is appealing to me. Just adding them to `GitRepo` and overriding in `AnnexRepo` would look strange in cases like `is_under_annex`.\n\nAgree?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1478599672,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTA5NjMyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259096321"},"message":"There is Repo already.\n\nOn Nov 8, 2016 11:06 AM, \"Benjamin Poldrack\" notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n\u003e Okay. So, let's grow that list and have a third class, that declares those\n\u003e (abstract). Then GitRepo and AnnexRepo have to implement them. That way\n\u003e that list would be easy to grow and maintain.\n\u003e And: I'd like to make it explicit, that these methods are supposed to work\n\u003e on both, while being implemented differently and while, at a first glance,\n\u003e some of them might not really make sense for a GitRepo. That's why a\n\u003e dedicated container for these \"result oriented cross repo methods\" is\n\u003e appealing to me. Just adding them to GitRepo and overriding in AnnexRepo\n\u003e would look strange in cases like is_under_annex.\n\u003e \n\u003e Agree?\n\u003e \n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259096047,\n\u003e or mute the thread\n\u003e https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIVHyydGXHgheplTRDXMGyXAUKTo-MFks5q8EmrgaJpZM4KsMt8\n\u003e .","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1478600146,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTA5ODEyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259098125"},"message":"I'm not sure what you are talking about. Do you mean `git.Repo`?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1478605076,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTExNDc4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-259114783"},"message":"Yeah, my bad. I was mistaking `gitrepo.Repo` for a class (because of the capitalization....).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486653537,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODY3MjQ1NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-278672455"},"message":"Started to actually work on that, but this raises questions.\n\nThe approach to let a `GitRepo ` answer the question `file_has_content` always with `True` (or `is_under_annex` with `False`) sounds reasonable at a first glance. But: Shouldn't it actually say \"I don't know\"?\n\nTo put in other words: It probably makes sense only, if we ensure that a `GitRepo` can not be instantiated while pointing to a physical annex repository. Otherwise it cannot derive a valid answer, I think.\nEnforcing this makes sense to me for another reason, too: The possibility to treat an actual annex as if it was a pure git by using an instance of `GitRepo` makes sense in V5 indirect mode only anyway.\n\nDo you agree @mih , @yarikoptic ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486717310,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg5MTgyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-278891823"},"message":"I agree, GitRepo pointing to a non-indirect V5 annex repo could have the potential to reek havoc.\n\nHowever, I am not convinced that we need to add extra measures to prevent it. Many use cases are absolutely OK -- in our own tests we use this quite a bit. Moreover, it is unlikely to happen during normal use.\n\n`GitRepo.file_has_content() -\u003e True` still makes sense to me. For all Git knows, a dead symlink is the content. Also GitRepo does not, and likely will never, test whether a particular git repo it is pointed to is fully capable of performing all functions we require -- we simply assume that, because it is most often true. Hence I consider it out-of-scope to have GitRepo test this particular aspect, when we test pretty much nothing else, and when it is only a problem for some part of the functionality.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486717643,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg5Mjg0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-278892846"},"message":"\u003e Moreover, it is unlikely to happen during normal use.\n\nProbably true, since we simply should use `Dataset.repo` in higher level functions.\nI'm fine with that, but we should be aware.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486718510,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg5NTc2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-278895766"},"message":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XkU23m6yX04\u0026t=1m27s","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1489656246,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4NzAwMDk5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-287000994"},"message":"Is this issue being addressed in any ongoing work?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1492100696,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5Mzk0ODQyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-293948425"},"message":"Found the RepoInterface and its sth_like_file_has_content in current code base and wondered either they are to stay or just be killed\nFWIW -- I am inline with @mih in https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-278891823","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1495194476,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjY4MjEyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-302682123"},"message":"FTR: We have passed the 6-month reconsideration period. It seems nothing speaks against:\n\n`GitRepo.file_has_content(whatever): return exists(whatever) and not isdir(whatever)`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1522951682,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3OTAyNjY0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-379026647"},"message":"@mih: Sounds good to us (@yarikoptic and @kyleam )","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523040418,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3OTM0Mjk2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-379342961"},"message":"Also see #2055","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524150534,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4Mjc3MjIwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-382772202"},"message":"FTR: If this get's fixed eventually, please grep for '#2055' and unuglify the code.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540748748,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzcyNjA1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1100#issuecomment-433726057"},"message":"I will take the liberty to close this (as the original author). In -revolution this has